{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/821184-death-note-as-infrastructure","id":821184,"title":"Death Note as Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-01T13:47:52-08:00","id":821184,"title":"Death Note as Infrastructure","content":"Is it just me, or would the Death Note be an excellent example of an artefact that appears to be magical but is in fact supported by Infrastructure? I man, the thing basically manipulates causality (something that the G-M is very good at doing) to cause people to die. Its conditions can fairly easily be taken advantage of and can be explained by the limits of the thing's supporting Infrasructure. Now that I think about it, the Shinigami could easily be angels (with Rem perhaps being one on the verge of falling). The Shinigami world itself could be the infrastructure perhaps?<br /> <br /> I could imagine this sparking off a plot in fact, with a mortal gaining possession of the Note and both the G-M and the Unchained rushing to first find out why the heck so many people are dying of heart attacks and then to claim the object itself (or at least deny it to the other side).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:59:23-08:00","id":821193,"title":"","content":"The Exploit 'Murder By Improbability' is already a Death Note and could easily be made into a literal Death Note as a gadget. The plot works really well, but (horrifyingly), the object has surprisingly limited value as a unique object in the setting. Still dangerous, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:15:03-08:00","id":821204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/821184-death-note-as-infrastructure?p=821193#post821193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exploit 'Murder By Improbability' is already a Death Note and could easily be made into a literal Death Note as a gadget. The plot works really well, but (horrifyingly), the object has surprisingly limited value as a unique object in the setting. Still dangerous, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I hadn't remembered that one. It could still kick-start a plot if a mortal was to get their hands on one though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:07:47-08:00","id":821233,"title":"","content":"In terms of describing the book's relationship to infrastructure, I think if it's involved in any projects, it is the infrastructure used by the shinigami, not the other way around. The infrastructure is the mechanism used to achieve an effect, and that's the book. Write name in book, person directly dies, no middleman to intercept. If the shinigami were the infrastructure, then Light writing a name in the book would compel Ryuk to go kill the person, rather than the book doing the killing. The shinigami just happen to be the entities that own and use the notebooks.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it's pretty much a Murder by Improbability gadget. Given how derelict and irresponsible the shinigami are in the series, and the ability to create gadgets, demons are probably a closer analogue than angels. If you look at them as angels, though, you could launch a whole story out of Rem experiencing the Fall, rather than simply dying, out of her loyalty to Misa.<br /> <br /> You're certainly right in that it's a gadget with tons of plot potential depending on who gets a hand on it. As an Exploited gadget, though, it's eventually going to run out of Aether. Is the human who has the book clued into how it works enough to figure out a countermeasure? Might she go about finding ways to use the book's murders indirectly, to trap and kill the Unchained and harvest them for Aether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:14:12-08:00","id":821237,"title":"","content":"It would certainly be interesting, and quite a wake-up call for the Unchained, having a human make deals with them from a position of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}